{
  "an6.60:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.60 ",
  "an6.60:0.2": "6. The Great Chapter ",
  "an6.60:0.3": "With Hatthisāriputta ",
  "an6.60:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an6.60:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Varanasi in the deer park at Isipatana. ",
  "an6.60:1.3": "Now at that time several senior mendicants, after the meal, on their return from almsround, sat together in the pavilion talking about the teachings. ",
  "an6.60:1.4": "Venerable Citta Hatthisāriputta interrupted them while they were talking. ",
  "an6.60:1.5": "Then Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita said to Venerable Citta Hatthisāriputta, ",
  "an6.60:1.6": "“Venerable, please don’t interrupt the senior mendicants while they’re talking about the teachings. Wait until the end of the discussion.” ",
  "an6.60:1.7": "When he said this, Citta Hatthisāriputta’s companions said to Mahākoṭṭhita, ",
  "an6.60:1.8": "“Venerable, please don’t rebuke Citta Hatthisāriputta. He is astute, ",
  "an6.60:1.9": "and quite capable of talking about the teachings with the senior mendicants.” ",
  "an6.60:2.1": "“It’s not easy to know this, reverends, for those who don’t encompass another’s mind. ",
  "an6.60:2.2": "Take an individual who is the gentlest of the gentle, the most placid of the placid, the calmest of the calm, so long as they live relying on the Teacher or a spiritual companion in a teacher’s role. ",
  "an6.60:2.3": "But when they’re separated from the Teacher or a spiritual companion in a teacher’s rol